        schema:contentUrl  <https://silknow.org/silknow/media/vam/O265549_0.jpg> , <http://media.vam.ac.uk/media/thira/collection_images/2020MR/2020MR7530.jpg> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/b6a5d7fe-7b19-38e8-bf2e-3ab762c6048f/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Textile fragment of woven silk. With a chinoiserie design in mauve damask and gold thread. The damask pattern consists of floral motifs and a jug from which water is pouring into a pitcher. The design shows a lion resting under a parasol with a palm tree on his right. This motif is connected by a tenuous sequence of bizarre shapes to a group of floral motifs and a small satyr carrying a torch.\n\nThe damask pattern is formed by a weft-faced twill on a satin of 5 warp-faced ground. The metal thread is brocaded and bound in 4/1 twill by a proportion of the warp threads. It is made from a silver gilt strip S wound on a yellow silk core. \n\nThe silk is make up from five fragments which have been joined together."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/b6a5d7fe-7b19-38e8-bf2e-3ab762c6048f> .

<https://sws.geonames.org/3017382/>
